            "coreRule": "A sigma bond has electron density along the internuclear axis. A pi bond comes from side-on p-orbital overlap. A double bond has one sigma and one pi; a triple bond has one sigma and two pi. Constructive overlap forms a lower-energy bonding MO; destructive overlap gives an antibonding MO with an added node.",
            "stepTopics": [
              "1. Double bond inventory",
              "2. Triple bond inventory"
